<%# locals: owner:, name:, subscription:, error: (optional)

    Watching a repository from the repository's own page — the same thing the
    form on /subscriptions does, from where someone actually stands when they
    decide they want it.

    It posts to the same two actions, with `from: "repo"`, which is what tells
    WebhookSubscriptionsController to send this control back in place instead
    of redirecting to /subscriptions. Every failure the registrar can raise
    lands in `error:` and is rendered right here, next to the button that
    caused it.

    The consent lives behind "What happens?" rather than beside the button: it
    is three sentences, and three sentences printed in a page header are noise
    to everyone who has not yet decided to click. A native <details> so it
    needs no JavaScript to open, is keyboard-reachable and touch-friendly for
    free, and adds no inline handler for the CSP to refuse; the `menu`
    controller only adds outside-click and Escape closing, exactly as the
    account menu and the reaction picker do.

    The panel is positioned against this element, not against the <details> —
    the trigger sits mid-row, so anchoring to it would hang the panel off the
    left of a phone screen. %>
<% error = local_assigns[:error] %>
<div id="repo-watch" class="relative flex min-w-0 basis-full flex-col items-end gap-1.5 text-right sm:flex-1 sm:basis-0"
     data-testid="repo-watch">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-2">
    <% if subscription %>
      <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/status_pill", subscription: subscription %>
    <% end %>

    <details data-controller="menu" data-testid="watch-explainer">
      <summary class="flex list-none items-center gap-1 rounded-lg px-2 py-1 font-display text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft hover:bg-sunk hover:text-ink">
        What happens?
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true">
          <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.22 8.22a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0L10 11.94l3.72-3.72a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-4.25 4.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0L5.22 9.28a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06Z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
        </svg>
      </summary>

      <div class="absolute right-0 top-full z-40 mt-1 w-72 max-w-full rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-3 text-left text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-soft shadow-lg shadow-ink/5"
           data-testid="watch-explainer-panel">
        <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/consent", login: current_user.login %>
      </div>
    </details>

    <% if subscription %>
      <% if subscription.callback_stale? %>
        <%= button_to "Re-register", webhook_subscription_path(subscription),
                      method: :patch,
                      params: { from: "repo" },
                      class: "btn-secondary",
                      data: { testid: "repo-re-register-button" } %>
      <% end %>

      <%= button_to "Stop watching", webhook_subscription_path(subscription),
                    method: :delete,
                    params: { from: "repo" },
                    class: "btn-danger",
                    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Stop watching #{subscription.full_name}? Prism will delete the webhook on GitHub. Links already added to pull requests stay where they are." } },
                    data: { testid: "repo-unwatch-button" } %>
    <% else %>
      <%= button_to "Watch repository", webhook_subscriptions_path,
                    params: { full_name: "#{owner}/#{name}", from: "repo" },
                    class: "btn-primary",
                    data: { testid: "repo-watch-button" } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# What is left in the open is only ever exceptional: a failure, or a
      subscription that has stopped working. Neither is something to tuck
      behind a disclosure. %>
  <% if error.present? %>
    <p role="alert" class="text-sm text-removed" data-testid="repo-watch-error"><%= error %></p>
  <% elsif subscription %>
    <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/status_reason", subscription: subscription %>
  <% end %>
</div>
